  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Get low to the rim – pick up the cone",
  "description": "Put one cone at the top just outside the three-point line and one at the elbow (where the free-throw line meets the lane). Players line up under the basket with a ball each. The player dribbles out to the top cone, goes round it and curls back towards the elbow. On the way past, the player picks up the cone with the free hand – which forces the hips down – and finishes straight away with a lay-up. Put the cone back and go to the end of the line.\n\nRun it from both the right and the left side so both hands get the work.\n\nVariations: make a change of direction right at the cone before picking it up – behind the back, crossover or between the legs. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Nose over toes and hips low as you pick up the cone – the same position as a first step past a defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep your speed through the curl round the top cone, short steps in the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Protect the ball with your body while you bend down."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish with the correct hand and foot: right side right hand, left side left hand."
    }
  ],
